[{:db/id "q-335207/selection/767f2d838c12b7681b6b919054f50eb72d8ad6412a3457782059b990e9338e8e" :answer/id #uuid "029b8c47-ff2a-569b-9948-76e2b4305751" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=3u(t)-v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335207/selection/b9e2985d5e27c96bcc5693219138f763ab05cbb1e43d80a33af7289b147d0a6e" :answer/id #uuid "f7533251-0e92-5a0f-b6d1-97ec22af0f0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=3u(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335207/selection/356186936b4a36157f3705da585e423f18edb09c5c73373f263ab3968eb4be52" :answer/id #uuid "9c3906ee-3ab9-559a-815b-f0505e130ead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=3u(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335207/selection/e1afa55b32110c69efebfefd890b4b8a803613b29c73eaecf7be4a2dcb5839a7" :answer/id #uuid "8b239660-ea2f-57ef-8308-1db194c55adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=3u(t)-v(t)+5 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335207/selection/19acca507966bbf7adec130b9c659352d3abee2951165ebb8e1dc168cca06510" :answer/id #uuid "739ca367-6dc8-5f21-bd75-0cb90375c1f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=3u(t)-v(t)-1 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t)+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335207/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33cc2c1f-6ccb-5b67-83ba-b364765306c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335207/selection/767f2d838c12b7681b6b919054f50eb72d8ad6412a3457782059b990e9338e8e" :answer-field/choices ["q-335207/selection/767f2d838c12b7681b6b919054f50eb72d8ad6412a3457782059b990e9338e8e" "q-335207/selection/b9e2985d5e27c96bcc5693219138f763ab05cbb1e43d80a33af7289b147d0a6e" "q-335207/selection/356186936b4a36157f3705da585e423f18edb09c5c73373f263ab3968eb4be52" "q-335207/selection/e1afa55b32110c69efebfefd890b4b8a803613b29c73eaecf7be4a2dcb5839a7" "q-335207/selection/19acca507966bbf7adec130b9c659352d3abee2951165ebb8e1dc168cca06510"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335207" :question/id #uuid "c89cb551-d1e6-5832-a074-6afc9561ced3" :question/math-academy-id "q-335207" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-y(t)+5 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[-1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTo shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=3u(t)-v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335207/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa4f5a7f-8008-5a23-a62e-54ceae2b1fe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335207"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335212/selection/27b087de9fe13e33ed857a4a83d4d7b8d2220008cee4fdd2c654380210ebbe2f" :answer/id #uuid "daad85e0-d252-5e46-b314-bb0bf8f4aa5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+3v(t)+4 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-u(t)+4v(t)+9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335212/selection/b746b233b21a3b473423d1cc03c70f82a95ea7116030ceb74060c4dec7605a13" :answer/id #uuid "286638f0-ecd3-51bf-b84d-8c8b0db4e9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+3v(t)+1 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-u(t)+4v(t)-1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335212/selection/431868864dd8b8a968da21f4a87c8157ef7591017c4d6148ffb2aade7f679015" :answer/id #uuid "38c83fd3-b49d-5c65-87b9-efaae9517320" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+3v(t)+1 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-u(t)+4v(t)+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335212/selection/5a80468e479ba121fd9640a6e309eb3fe5b3c83a741080fea590e302c6ae6d2a" :answer/id #uuid "90d55b8b-5ae4-53cf-9459-316b8cdb95a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2u(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=4v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335212/selection/775d75f3589c6640de2f392d6d50469d5b7331a4406310bba911077ff5c12eb2" :answer/id #uuid "265879b9-a4ba-534b-b65d-81d959c3ca67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-u(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335212/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "41cbc6ff-2e9a-534c-826d-cd46e55f9095" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335212/selection/775d75f3589c6640de2f392d6d50469d5b7331a4406310bba911077ff5c12eb2" :answer-field/choices ["q-335212/selection/27b087de9fe13e33ed857a4a83d4d7b8d2220008cee4fdd2c654380210ebbe2f" "q-335212/selection/b746b233b21a3b473423d1cc03c70f82a95ea7116030ceb74060c4dec7605a13" "q-335212/selection/431868864dd8b8a968da21f4a87c8157ef7591017c4d6148ffb2aade7f679015" "q-335212/selection/5a80468e479ba121fd9640a6e309eb3fe5b3c83a741080fea590e302c6ae6d2a" "q-335212/selection/775d75f3589c6640de2f392d6d50469d5b7331a4406310bba911077ff5c12eb2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335212" :question/id #uuid "cc6d171a-592a-572e-86fe-d9a714207d33" :question/math-academy-id "q-335212" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+3y(t)+4 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t)+4y(t)+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,-2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTo shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-u(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335212/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa4f5a7f-8008-5a23-a62e-54ceae2b1fe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335212"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335079/selection/e2b2dc0f94619c4b286b39763b49b317a009f05517a2ecfcc04f1c675ea48ed1" :answer/id #uuid "1acf55d8-57a6-5043-9ce8-a1270510b072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335079/selection/4a59c3b2c2a50e6fb22d426270ff5c2b7d8d6c405831c47e18b3dc4e07eed7da" :answer/id #uuid "ff4c5aeb-cce8-549c-847f-5ed4e539340e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335079/selection/e7ae91829e6ede9daaf3c64dcf367772423df7b20a5725a6cc90d4782cab063f" :answer/id #uuid "b15b9e36-afe7-5769-90b3-e6f164d4ef0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]u" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335079/selection/70390dcdf22a2f152e24c03cd9a537afe163211064251fea8f0cf08c7838eb20" :answer/id #uuid "a7e73b11-d675-558f-8da1-01027085bcb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]u" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335079/selection/2876564faa423f6b0d7cfe482c2341c34a841d70ce5c2784127b55cd52a54d80" :answer/id #uuid "7eb69658-745e-5351-b689-5a5cee1a83c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]u" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335079/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d8debf3-5e9e-53f0-92a3-048fa2f7f0bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335079/selection/70390dcdf22a2f152e24c03cd9a537afe163211064251fea8f0cf08c7838eb20" :answer-field/choices ["q-335079/selection/e2b2dc0f94619c4b286b39763b49b317a009f05517a2ecfcc04f1c675ea48ed1" "q-335079/selection/4a59c3b2c2a50e6fb22d426270ff5c2b7d8d6c405831c47e18b3dc4e07eed7da" "q-335079/selection/e7ae91829e6ede9daaf3c64dcf367772423df7b20a5725a6cc90d4782cab063f" "q-335079/selection/70390dcdf22a2f152e24c03cd9a537afe163211064251fea8f0cf08c7838eb20" "q-335079/selection/2876564faa423f6b0d7cfe482c2341c34a841d70ce5c2784127b55cd52a54d80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335079" :question/id #uuid "8cd87a99-e6c2-5b74-be33-b608333e4e71" :question/math-academy-id "q-335079" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[2,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?" :question/worked-solution "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]u.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335079/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa4f5a7f-8008-5a23-a62e-54ceae2b1fe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335079"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335073/selection/ff3a02d0e19af96c203b2215b83ae9a281d85ececde19cd3f34dfabbb8ff284e" :answer/id #uuid "ccdba148-7431-50d3-afcf-a699cdd44139" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]u" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335073/selection/b3016de0f7a1941ab92d55c85bc9455e486957e04c1ee2e973a7869334a684dd" :answer/id #uuid "ec13fc6b-2566-51c7-aa36-8b702b9d6b91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335073/selection/73efe78f627e861fa3d0b87f4b1c4402ae120e9b0e43500c1e235df14742c9a0" :answer/id #uuid "1e15e928-0a5d-5289-8a22-f7f263438642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 &