n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]u.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335073/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa4f5a7f-8008-5a23-a62e-54ceae2b1fe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335073"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335213/selection/6b9d38d9cd6c2e0ebac5cf1f7f499f6e248a704e95b46845fa6fd456f9abcf41" :answer/id #uuid "ad4d0af5-449f-5017-ac3c-441273db7eb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)+v(t)+1 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+5v(t)+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335213/selection/5daecb7849ca72c9545b32e4f113ed12ff9dab2449066924ce1b5c987caf1cd3" :answer/id #uuid "35ae5acc-f0e7-5763-b9ea-ee3190bbb38a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)+v(t)+5 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+5v(t)-9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335213/selection/8eccdad7d307f342969e08841efaaf5b3bae3397c600ed302a6e1a8bb43ddf24" :answer/id #uuid "4b8c241c-004f-5771-826a-6d831d71bdd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+5v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335213/selection/e3c71aa5fb572e68e0fd96dc1a15e3a13ba07627aca52020a84eb471ac03d6c6" :answer/id #uuid "1b4ac630-af78-5e27-9532-4fd52cee3768" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)+v(t)+2 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+5v(t)-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335213/selection/345334d7764d4d843331428684e01d110b80e50c2ecef409f7e03350ad72a830" :answer/id #uuid "dfae2756-bebf-5a94-9565-53164f718823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=-3u(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=5v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335213/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9425db89-bdf8-5171-9caa-91f8d8a00051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335213/selection/8eccdad7d307f342969e08841efaaf5b3bae3397c600ed302a6e1a8bb43ddf24" :answer-field/choices ["q-335213/selection/6b9d38d9cd6c2e0ebac5cf1f7f499f6e248a704e95b46845fa6fd456f9abcf41" "q-335213/selection/5daecb7849ca72c9545b32e4f113ed12ff9dab2449066924ce1b5c987caf1cd3" "q-335213/selection/8eccdad7d307f342969e08841efaaf5b3bae3397c600ed302a6e1a8bb43ddf24" "q-335213/selection/e3c71aa5fb572e68e0fd96dc1a15e3a13ba07627aca52020a84eb471ac03d6c6" "q-335213/selection/345334d7764d4d843331428684e01d110b80e50c2ecef409f7e03350ad72a830"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335213" :question/id #uuid "745434e5-21ff-571f-b4ba-3dac76316242" :question/math-academy-id "q-335213" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t)+5 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+5y(t)-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[2,\\,1]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTo shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=-3u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+5v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335213/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa4f5a7f-8008-5a23-a62e-54ceae2b1fe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335213"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335384/selection/8316d6adef9390baf87115897eda739730978e87cd49ba1aaadd4177eee3bd26" :answer/id #uuid "1bd4d559-dc25-5ef2-8407-480e9c115e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335384/selection/152a30e84ec67a573fd77c4baaf458d7e11e366ce6b2e405bb97c3e9e591f116" :answer/id #uuid "0a8d7b1e-f9f7-5cbd-8331-b5fd992f97a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335384/selection/7db6fcd1f26e2102ab5a6f006b73b591439fc8f5a97c12bef4def6ff6175a72f" :answer/id #uuid "844b645b-fa5f-50c8-95ca-0b1af1175158" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335384/selection/080ee436223a0a9852322aa255971df3592f607b9ffae43f641448fecf8b7bd0" :answer/id #uuid "b1b6e477-ee48-59cc-984f-c7d8564f93d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-2{v}^{2}(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335384/selection/ef527e0244cf896fd063b0d04d16cadf010252fdd6df74e1eff114736a6f43f0" :answer/id #uuid "659bd375-d3e1-5d3e-b3c9-7305b116c4e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=u(t)+2{u}^{2}(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335384/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c49f71d1-d62a-54ed-b247-f377b497850b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335384/selection/8316d6adef9390baf87115897eda739730978e87cd49ba1aaadd4177eee3bd26" :answer-field/choices ["q-335384/selection/8316d6adef9390baf87115897eda739730978e87cd49ba1aaadd4177eee3bd26" "q-335384/selection/152a30e84ec67a573fd77c4baaf458d7e11e366ce6b2e405bb97c3e9e591f116" "q-335384/selection/7db6fcd1f26e2102ab5a6f006b73b591439fc8f5a97c12bef4def6ff6175a72f" "q-335384/selection/080ee436223a0a9852322aa255971df3592f607b9ffae43f641448fecf8b7bd0" "q-335384/selection/ef527e0244cf896fd063b0d04d16cadf010252fdd6df74e1eff114736a6f43f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335384" :question/id #uuid "e77fea41-127f-5d8e-ade7-a3fd6550869a" :question/math-academy-id "q-335384" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)+4x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+8y(t)-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[-1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" :question/worked-solution "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t)-1,\\,y(t)=v(t)+2,\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)+4x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =(u(t)-1)^{2}+4(u(t)-1)+(v(t)+2)+1 \\\\  & =({u}^{2}(t)-2u(t)+1)+4u(t)-4+v(t)+2+1 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =2x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+8y(t)-10 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =2(u(t)-1)-(v(t)+2)^{2}+8(v(t)+2)-10 \\\\  & =2u(t)-2-({v}^{2}(t)+4v(t)+4)+8v(t)+16-10 \\\\  & =2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+4v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :ques