er-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335478/selection/7c04f102c451daff4960eefba84007039a743a996b42a3b77ffb43243afbe80b" :answer-field/choices ["q-335478/selection/633f6f789c0bfed7d4ccf44f12ff05c48e6252600375ae79ae1890568d929ab4" "q-335478/selection/7c04f102c451daff4960eefba84007039a743a996b42a3b77ffb43243afbe80b" "q-335478/selection/18fed57702cf2feab76cb5eb9a5f84586b332c3ac155acf5c5a7636ef223ce2f" "q-335478/selection/66134890a17c792f35d5e4b349c48be25bd4dd29faf0a878f8e61ba3fc954c0a" "q-335478/selection/4725df5b453f0b79687f935ae62dbf0aa8f777b3c5f736787c6387c2f13505da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335478" :question/id #uuid "83e2b1e4-9301-5667-8010-f374b0cce368" :question/math-academy-id "q-335478" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)-6x(t)+2y(t)+9 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+y(t)-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[3,\\,0]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" :question/worked-solution "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t)+3,\\,y(t)=v(t),\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)-6x(t)+2y(t)+9 \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =(u(t)+3)^{2}-6(u(t)+3)+2v(t)+9 \\\\  & =({u}^{2}(t)+6u(t)+9)-6u(t)-18+2v(t)+9 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+2v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =4x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+y(t)-12 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =4(u(t)+3)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)-12 \\\\  & =4u(t)+12-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)-12 \\\\  & =4u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=4u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335478/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c6e6984-7029-5e3e-bfcc-b8e553658911"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335478"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335376/selection/3446fc3a3f6f94ef60e5956a3c7d42ea4a94d37a3cc13e7a526e2578b92a810d" :answer/id #uuid "9188e0ec-e72e-5afd-b816-fff0084e3a27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335376/selection/fe748e6ba75094dbc0b31421c4472893d0697151f57177c7c331b5c42c070584" :answer/id #uuid "bec9d762-104b-5b4b-aaca-6c310c7e082f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335376/selection/ac30e798838ae4e9c265790d544eb91d2508662f3040536c754db58725018932" :answer/id #uuid "d3af0b59-09f6-5c61-8c22-8c062e45d157" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335376/selection/f96a77f082de32497a33b08c9ab654ded31c15da8d5946e02643bb7e38f5084b" :answer/id #uuid "b8d894a1-c838-5f3a-a491-1c93ebcf87ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335376/selection/ebd70c26fa32d9f2135c9928afa692f3c1e3856f2cdf2910d02054ff55a55000" :answer/id #uuid "6cc03e38-f0ae-5637-9454-a4b493c9c081" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335376/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "376b025c-b442-5883-8af3-db664c1161c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335376/selection/f96a77f082de32497a33b08c9ab654ded31c15da8d5946e02643bb7e38f5084b" :answer-field/choices ["q-335376/selection/3446fc3a3f6f94ef60e5956a3c7d42ea4a94d37a3cc13e7a526e2578b92a810d" "q-335376/selection/fe748e6ba75094dbc0b31421c4472893d0697151f57177c7c331b5c42c070584" "q-335376/selection/ac30e798838ae4e9c265790d544eb91d2508662f3040536c754db58725018932" "q-335376/selection/f96a77f082de32497a33b08c9ab654ded31c15da8d5946e02643bb7e38f5084b" "q-335376/selection/ebd70c26fa32d9f2135c9928afa692f3c1e3856f2cdf2910d02054ff55a55000"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335376" :question/id #uuid "ce9aec9d-c2f9-599b-b8da-3b93db4c1e9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-335376" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)-x(t)+y(t)-2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+3y(t)-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[0,\\,2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" :question/worked-solution "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t),\\,y(t)=v(t)+2,\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)-x(t)+y(t)-2 \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+(v(t)+2)-2 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =2x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+3y(t)-2 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =2u(t)-(v(t)+2)^{2}+3(v(t)+2)-2 \\\\  & =2u(t)-({v}^{2}(t)+4v(t)+4)+3v(t)+6-2 \\\\  & =2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)-v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335376/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c6e6984-7029-5e3e-bfcc-b8e553658911"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335376"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335371/selection/3446fc3a3f6f94ef60e5956a3c7d42ea4a94d37a3cc13e7a526e2578b92a810d" :answer/id #uuid "5301ce5c-5f44-50f9-a62d-0eb5d4a59ffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335371/selection/b17df199a0d7a67df91d25e3f974b421e5329cf37d4de5f3183311aaecd9adb6" :answer/id #uuid "4be061e3-eee9-5d37-b538-efe82fcd99b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335371/selection/da217ef0d654770964101fb44d8683bfabb2df26ed6826dad0afd00c985da103" :answer/id #uuid "13d836c5-6bcc-54c1-9b8f-5f3a7899ecb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=2{u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335371/selection/cbab7c32c7556d4057e63cd9268573f537290dc0cae61898d97df3c3b3b7bef9" :answer/id #uuid "ecfab591-dd48-5163-985f-369bfebc5aff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335371/selection/b5bf6ba165338b1ae9215fbc60f3d67895bbf2af99c76487fe4acbdcf9aadfad" :answer/id #uuid "4587dacc-b60d-5373-82e7-0fc9fc817ba4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335371/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfaa1055-44a7-52d2-9117-2a111fc46aae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335371/selection/b17df199a0d7a67df91d25e3f974b421e5329cf37d4de5f3183311aaecd9adb6" :answer-field/choices ["q-335371/selection/3446fc3a3f6f94ef60e5956a3c7d42ea4a94d37a3cc13e7a526e2578b92a810d" "q-335371/selection/b17df199a0d7a67df91d25e3f974b421e5329cf37d4de5f3183311aaecd9adb6" "q-335371/selection/da217ef0d654770964101fb44d8683bfabb2df26ed6826dad0afd00c985da103" "q-335371/selection/cbab7c32c7556d4057e63cd9268573f537290dc0cae61898d97df3c3b3b7bef9" "q-335371/selection/b5bf6ba165338b1ae9215fbc60f3d67895bbf2af99c76487fe4acbdcf9aadfad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335371" :question/id #uuid "9934bc5f-ba47-56cd-bf7b-e37132886f6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-335371" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)+y(t)-2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+3y(t)-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,1]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" :question/worked-solution "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $u=[\\begin{aligned}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t)+1,\\,y(t)=v(t)+1,\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)+y(t)-2 \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =(u(t)+1)^{2}+(v(t)+1)-2 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+1+v(t)+1-2 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =2x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+3y(t)-4 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =2(u(t)+1)-(v(t)+1)^{2}+3(v(t)+1)-4 \\\\  & =2u(t)+2-({v}^{2}(t)+2v(t)+1)+3v(t)+3-4 \\\\  & =2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335371/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c6e6984-7029-5e3e-bfcc-b8e553658911"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335371"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186221914 :question/answer-fields 17592186220435] {:db/id "q-333671/selection/ma-v1/efc9608fe3ff99f7525e0771511c3d04c2cf428422907011e12db51b1e5f01b5/e69d6de10c3b2364842453efd10aa50b6c7bc9953b5bb881acc970bf60f618be" :answer/id #uuid "e70b268c-fee7-584c-a5a4-696f0ad31e07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)=u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=3{u}^{2}(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333671/selection/ma-v1/efc9608fe3ff99f7525e0771511c3d04c2cf428422907011e12db51b1e5f01b5/5a59af3f38b017545e7